    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0930" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/307: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-27T11:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                                1921—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:28
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>142. For Mr. Sumner Welles.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d752-f1"/></p>
                <p>I think President Zayas in substantial accord with you, has a proposition to
                    abolish Sugar Finance Commission at once rather than wait until February 1st as
                    originally contemplated. At our last conference it [was] suggested [that] it
                    would be advisable before <pb facs="0931" n="807" xml:id="pg807"/> issuing a
                    decree of this character to consult the owners of the carryover sugar. I have
                    for several days contemplated that a decree abolishing said Commission would be
                    issued at an early date with the approval of said owners and the consent of both
                    Governments.</p>
                <p>Respecting the tariff, public opinion here continues chaotic but an effort is
                    being made to secure a study and report upon an <hi rendition="#italic">ad
                        valorcm</hi> tariff. Have held important conferences in the last few days
                    [in] supreme effort to consolidate Cuban public opinion in favor of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad valorem</hi> duty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d752-f1" n="1" xml:id="d752-f1-content">
